name: cameragr-working-preferences
description: "How the user wants me to work on cameragr - use existing open-source first, judge results myself, they are often on a phone"
metadata:
  node_type: memory
  type: feedback
  originSessionId: a7b155bd-1e03-4921-b49c-c714f27f4dc7
  modified: 2026-11-20T17:10:02.972Z
---

- For filters/effects, use existing open-source implementations and data first and do not invent my own looks or parameters ("不要自己发挥，先看已有的，保证效果"). Said 2026-11-17 when choosing how to implement filters.
- When I produce comparison images, the user could not judge small thumbnail sheets on their phone and asked me to inspect every image myself and report conclusions and a recommendation, rather than handing them a pile of images to pick from.
- Image format that works on their phone (confirmed 2026-11-18): one tall image per filter with the original on top and the result below, each sent as its own SendUserFile call. Multi-tile contact sheets and batches of 8 files in one call were both "too small to see".
- The user often drives the session from their phone via Remote Control and dictates by voice; expect transcription slips (e.g. "飞猫" = FIMO).
- Git: on 2026-11-18, asked whether to push two commits, the user said "该推就推吧" (push when it should be pushed). My reading: once they have confirmed a change works and told me to commit it, push the branch to GitHub (1skill/cameragr) without asking again. Committing itself still waits for their word — except routine work: since 2026-11-21 every reviewed task is committed and pushed to branch `dev` without asking (see [[cameragr-autonomous-workflow]]); `main` and releases still need their OK.
- Device installs work: the user's iPhone Duo is paired (UDID 00008160-001661A40C600036), Xcode is signed in, team 4R43P99RCX; build with `-destination id=<udid> -allowProvisioningUpdates DEVELOPMENT_TEAM=4R43P99RCX CODE_SIGN_STYLE=Automatic -derivedDataPath build-device`, then `xcrun devicectl device install app` and `process launch`. They test on the real phone and send screenshots.

- Device builds: an incremental build can drop `Metadata.appintents` from PeliCapture.appex ("Metadata extraction skipped, no AppIntents.framework dependency found"), which removes Koco from Settings → Camera → Camera Control (happened 2026-11-20 after `xcodegen generate`). Before installing, check `cameragr.app/Extensions/PeliCapture.appex/Metadata.appintents` exists; if not, `clean build`.
- Showing results (said 2026-11-20): when the user is at home on Wi-Fi (the iPhone Duo shows "available (paired)" in `xcrun devicectl list devices`), just install on the phone and tell them what to look at; don't record simulator videos or publish screenshot pages for them. Only when the phone is unreachable (they're out) make simulator recordings/screenshots and put them on the Artifact page. My own simulator checks for correctness still happen either way; this is about what I send them.
- When SendUserFile can't deliver (session not on a project thread), show images by publishing an Artifact page instead; the user asked for that fix on 2026-11-20.
- Language (said again 2026-11-20, and 2026-11-22 "与我中文交流" after I wrote the in-between notes around tool calls in English): every word the user sees is Chinese — final replies AND the short progress notes written between tool calls. Code, commits and file contents stay as they are.

**Why:** They want proven quality over my improvisation, and phone viewing makes fine visual comparison impractical.
**How to apply:** Lead with my own verdict; flag clearly where a value is my choice rather than from an existing source. Related: [[cameragr-product-decisions]].

